<http://data.silknow.org/object/f69f7ec2-fc9a-30b3-ac9b-c639089a6894/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Two fragments from a piece, full width. Copperplate engraving, printed in brown on cotton cloth. When assembled, two fragments show full repeat. Main scene, at center, shows two ladies talking with a girl in a park; at the right, two ladies converse with a gentleman at the foot of a flight of stone steps with balustrade. Above, at left, two ladies being rowed in a boat by a man, past gothic ruins; at right, a lady and gentleman strilling in woods. Inscribed on edge of tread of bottom step: \"Drawn and Engrav'd By D. Richards (s reversed) Manch.r.\" Cotton darkened and brittle; many holes and tears; darning."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f69f7ec2-fc9a-30b3-ac9b-c639089a6894> .

